1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Mixed umbrella (ETF and non-ETF sub-funds):** The umbrella name need not include \"UCITS ETF\". Each ETF sub-fund must carry the identifier in its name, prospectus/supplement, KID and marketing communications. Non-ETF sub-funds must not use it, and documents should clearly separate the two.\n\n**Sub-fund with listed and unlisted classes:** The Central Bank of Ireland permits ETF status at share-class level. The identifier then goes in the **names of the listed (ETF) classes**, not the sub-fund name, so unlisted classes aren't described as ETFs. The supplement should state which classes are ETF classes and explain dealing differences, such as primary-market access versus direct subscription and redemption.\n\n**Key point:** An all-ETF sub-fund is identified at sub-fund level. A mixed sub-fund is identified at class level. Non-ETF siblings, whether sub-funds or classes, are never labelled \"UCITS ETF\".\n\nCheck the latest CBI UCITS Q&A for current wording.","ttft_ms":1389,"type":"result","duration_ms":3749,"uuid":"9aa70c43-08a2-4c1d-9985-02397c08f023","ttft_stream_ms":1215,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":1216,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
